md='''# Independent PBPS centered-root preread64

This is a source-backed proposed route, not a theorem, proof credit, SAU claim, Statement Seal or source review of science63. The independent graph was sealed before reading current production/APIs. Root remains sole canonical writer.

The exact source is arXiv:2609.06905v1, pinned raw SHA256 **d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760**. Ten literal regions retain zero-based half-open byte ranges, raw/LF bytes, rendered formula alttext and hashes in `primary-regions-receipt.json`. The independent graph and 1086-item exhaustive classified inventory have hashes in `source-first-graph-seal.json`; no math alttext is missing. B10-B16, 1.1, 2.6-2.7, C1-C4, D1/order/root conventions and downstream Appendix C.2/C.3 hypotheses are retained. Excluded branches carry reasons.

## Proposed smallest mathematical packet

Prove a generic arbitrary-measure REAL L2 positive-square-order adapter and use it to prove the printed B15 order of the SAME actual macroscopic root on **H_P,0**, together with its internally derived bounded inverse. Source binders remain the original C2 potential, both global Hessian bounds, 0<alpha<=beta, eta>0 and beta eta<=1, plus established Euclidean/finite-real-Hilbert typing. Rank0 is the disclosed extension; alpha eta=1 remains legal. No hGap/hRoot/hOnto/hUnit, higher derivative, finite L2 or Nontrivial premise is allowed.

Writing T=U_PP, L=U_perpP and Gamma=(I-T²)^(1/2), the source proof is

    eta ||gradient Tf||² <= (1-alpha eta)²/[4(1+alpha eta)] ||Lf||²       (C2)
    ||Tf||² <= (1/alpha+eta)||gradient Tf||²                           (C3, centered)
    ||Tf|| <= rho ||f||, rho=(1-alpha eta)/(1+alpha eta)                 (C4)
    Gamma0² >= delta I, delta=4alpha eta/(1+alpha eta)²
    Gamma0 >= gamma I, gamma=2sqrt(alpha eta)/(1+alpha eta)>0             (B15)

The last implication is positive square-root monotonicity, not merely a lower norm estimate. The independent -1/2 lower-spectrum branch of full B14 and the half-turn C.2/C.3 branches are not B15 parents. At alpha eta=1 the proof keeps rho=0 and gamma=1; no denominator 1-alpha eta may be introduced.

## Internally derived adapters, in seven steps

'''
